# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model) offers new tools for inspecting and customizing error mitigation workflow** &mdash; New tools have been built on top of the directed execution model framework, which was released earlier this year:\n"
msgstr "**Nag-aalok ang [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model) ng mga bagong tool para siyasatin at i-customize ang error mitigation workflow** &mdash; May mga bagong tool na binuo sa ibabaw ng framework ng directed execution model, na inilabas nang mas maaga ngayong taon:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Together with [Samplomatic](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/samplomatic/index), they make up the [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model), which provides full transparency and control to fine-tune your error mitigation workflow. The [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/tutorials/01_getting_started.html) tutorial, for example, demonstrates how this model is used to combine advanced techniques, including shaded lightcones, probabilistic error cancellation (PEC), Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX), and [measurement-based postselection](/guides/post-selection), to further improve the result quality.\n"
"  - [`qiskit-noise-learning`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-noise-learning) is a toolkit for randomization-based quantum noise characterization. You can use it to construct a custom noise-learning experiment, validate it with local simulation, and analyze the raw results.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Kasama ang [Samplomatic](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/samplomatic/index), bumubuo sila ng [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model), na nagbibigay ng buong transparency at control upang i-fine-tune ang iyong error mitigation workflow. Ang tutorial na [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/tutorials/01_getting_started.html), halimbawa, ay nagpapakita kung paano ginagamit ang model na ito upang pagsamahin ang mga advanced na teknik, kasama ang shaded lightcones, probabilistic error cancellation (PEC), Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX), at [measurement-based postselection](/guides/post-selection), upang mas mapabuti ang kalidad ng resulta.\n"
"  - Ang [`qiskit-noise-learning`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-noise-learning) ay isang toolkit para sa randomization-based na quantum noise characterization. Magagamit mo ito para bumuo ng custom na noise-learning experiment, i-validate ito gamit ang local simulation, at suriin ang mga raw na resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`qiskit-mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) is a package of quantum error mitigation methods for building mitigation pipelines with the new execution model. It includes implementations of well-known methods, including PEC, PEA, TREX, and gate-folding ZNE, as well as post-selection for filtering out non-Markovian errors.\n"
msgstr "Ang [`qiskit-mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) ay isang package ng mga paraan ng quantum error mitigation para sa pagbuo ng mga mitigation pipeline gamit ang bagong execution model. Kasama rito ang mga implementasyon ng mga kilalang paraan, kabilang ang PEC, PEA, TREX, at gate-folding ZNE, pati na rin ang post-selection para sa pag-filter ng mga non-Markovian na error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/release-notes#0500-2026-09-24) released **new client-side implementations of Sampler and Estimator** primitives that are built on top of this framework. These implementations allow you to inspect exactly how each error mitigation method is implemented and test them [locally](/guides/local-testing-mode) before running them on an actual QPU. \n"
msgstr "Inilabas ng [`qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/release-notes#0500-2026-09-24) ang **mga bagong client-side na implementasyon ng mga primitive na Sampler at Estimator** na binuo sa ibabaw ng framework na ito. Pinapayagan ka ng mga implementasyong ito na siyasatin nang eksakto kung paano ini-implement ang bawat paraan ng error mitigation at subukan ang mga ito [nang lokal](/guides/local-testing-mode) bago patakbuhin sa totoong QPU. \n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    **How to upgrade to the new primitives:** Upgrading to the new primitives is designed to be low-friction, so in most cases, you only need to change your import statements &mdash; not the body of your code. See the [migration guide](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) for full details.\n"
msgstr "    **Paano mag-upgrade sa mga bagong primitive:** Dinisenyo ang pag-upgrade sa mga bagong primitive para maging madali, kaya sa karamihan ng kaso, ang mga import statement lang ang kailangan mong baguhin &mdash; hindi ang nilalaman ng iyong code. Tingnan ang [migration guide](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) para sa buong detalye.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**New skills for agents** &mdash; Whether you are migrating to the new client-side Sampler and Estimator, or migrating old notebooks that still use V1 primitives, the migrate-qiskit-ibm-runtime skill in the [Qiskit/skills](https://github.com/Qiskit/skills) repository can simplify the task. This new open-source repository contains official, IBM-verified agent skills for building IBM Quantum and Qiskit workflows. We will be adding more skills to this repository in the near future.\n"
msgstr "**Mga bagong skill para sa mga agent** &mdash; Maging ikaw ay nagma-migrate sa bagong client-side na Sampler at Estimator, o nagma-migrate ng mga lumang notebook na gumagamit pa ng V1 primitives, mapapadali ng skill na migrate-qiskit-ibm-runtime sa repository na [Qiskit/skills](https://github.com/Qiskit/skills) ang gawain. Naglalaman ang bagong open-source na repository na ito ng mga opisyal at IBM-verified na agent skill para sa pagbuo ng mga workflow ng IBM Quantum at Qiskit. Magdaragdag kami ng higit pang skill sa repository na ito sa malapit na hinaharap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lastly, check out the [PEC with logical noise models tutorial](/tutorials/probabilistic-error-cancellation-with-logical-noise-models) for an example of stacking error detection and mitigation methods using these new tools.\n"
msgstr "Panghuli, tingnan ang [PEC with logical noise models tutorial](/tutorials/probabilistic-error-cancellation-with-logical-noise-models) para sa halimbawa ng pagsasalansan ng mga paraan ng error detection at mitigation gamit ang mga bagong tool na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The directed execution model, comprised of [Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/) and [Executor](/guides/get-started-with-executor), exposes the error mitigation logic applied to your workloads so that you have full control over the logic without sacrificing performance.\n"
msgstr "  Ang directed execution model, na binubuo ng [Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/) at [Executor](/guides/get-started-with-executor), ay naglalantad ng lohika ng error mitigation na inilalapat sa iyong mga workload para magkaroon ka ng buong kontrol sa lohikang iyon nang hindi isinasakripisyo ang performance.\n"

